 "statement": {
  "status": "present",
  "value": "grid is a rectangle of 0 (empty) and 1 (obstacle); teleports is a list of [r1, c1, r2, c2] rows: entering cell (r1, c1) instantly moves the robot to (r2, c2). The robot starts at (0, 0) and wants (n-1, m-1). Repeat: if the robot is at the destination, stop; if it is in the last column, or the cell to its right is an obstacle, it is stuck; otherwise it moves one cell right (one move) and, if that cell is a teleport entrance, is moved to the exit at no cost. If the robot ever returns to a position it already occupied it loops forever. Return the number of right moves needed to reach the destination, or -1 if it gets stuck or loops. Entrances are distinct empty cells; exits are empty cells that are not entrances; the start and the destination are empty and not entrances.",
  "provenance": [
   {
    "repository": "gamma",
    "revision": null,
